# Context

We previously discouraged using backticks for conceptual terms. We want precise, linkable references to concepts while preserving backticks for code/paths.

# Decision

Use backticks together with hashtagged terms for explicit concept references (e.g., `#always`, `#mind-theory`). Avoid backticks for plain prose concepts. Continue using backticks for code, commands, file paths.

# Consequences

- Improves precision: agents can distinguish conceptual references from prose.
- Enables consistent interlinking across tasks/rules/runbooks using shortcodes.
- Requires updating the notation rule in `./.cursor/rules/dict.mdc`.

# Alternatives Considered

- Never using backticks for concepts at all: too limiting and ambiguous.
- Using custom brackets without backticks: less consistent with code-style references.

